  "details": "PLEASE UPVOTE! someone has already put in a request. but it was back in 2021. I want to re-ignite this as this is something that has been stopping me from making a rocket launcher that plays audio when a mesh particle (for example), hits a collider/trigger VIA by parameter.\n\nSo far this is the ONLY thing holding me and plenty of others back! see, you would naturally just do a contact system that is triggered with a false state on a receiver when the particle system is turned off. but the only issue is that WRITE DEFAULTS are REQUIRED OFF! And now-a-days, every asset in VRC is made with WD ON... and you cant merge WD OFF with WD ON (Obviously).\n\nSo can we PLEASSSEEEE get a script that is say for example \"VRC Particle Collision Parameter\" that either works as a Driver in the animator or as a component.... This could literally be a game changer!\n\nThere is one AMAZING example that has been \"Tracked\" But no motion, so please go bump this or the other post (blow) and bump that up!\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/expose-particlephysicsextensions-that-helps-particle-collision-detection",
